# Domain Models and Data Structures

## 1. What are Domain Models?

**Domain Models** represent business entities and concepts in the application, encapsulating business logic and rules.

**Key Principle**: Domain models represent the business domain, not just data structures

### Data Structures vs Domain Models

**Data Structures** (DTOs):
```csharp
public class VesselDto  // ❌ Just data
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public string Status { get; set; }
}
```

**Domain Models**:
```csharp
public class Vessel  // ✅ Business entity with behavior
{
    public int Id { get; private set; }
    public string Name { get; private set; }
    public VesselStatus Status { get; private set; }
    
    public void Activate()  // ✅ Business logic
    {
        if (Status == VesselStatus.Active)
            throw new InvalidOperationException("Vessel is already active");
        
        Status = VesselStatus.Active;
    }
}
```

