## 2. Entity vs Value Object

### Entity

**Entity**: Object with identity that persists over time

**Characteristics**:
- Has unique identity (ID)
- Mutable (can change)
- Compared by identity
- Persisted in database

**MaritimeIQ Example**:
```csharp
public class Vessel
{
    public int Id { get; private set; }  // ✅ Identity
    public string Name { get; private set; }
    public VesselStatus Status { get; private set; }
    
    // Entities are compared by ID
    public override bool Equals(object? obj)
    {
        return obj is Vessel vessel && Id == vessel.Id;
    }
}
```

### Value Object

**Value Object**: Immutable object defined by its attributes

**Characteristics**:
- No identity (compared by value)
- Immutable (cannot change)
- Compared by all attributes
- Can be replaced

**MaritimeIQ Example**:
```csharp
public class Position  // ✅ Value object
{
    public double Latitude { get; }
    public double Longitude { get; }
    
    public Position(double latitude, double longitude)
    {
        if (latitude < -90 || latitude > 90)
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid latitude");
        if (longitude < -180 || longitude > 180)
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid longitude");
        
        Latitude = latitude;
        Longitude = longitude;
    }
    
    // Value objects are compared by all attributes
    public override bool Equals(object? obj)
    {
        return obj is Position position &&
               Latitude == position.Latitude &&
               Longitude == position.Longitude;
    }
}
```

