## 4. Data Transfer Objects (DTOs)

### What are DTOs?

**DTOs** are simple data structures used to transfer data between layers, without business logic.

**Purpose**:
- Transfer data across boundaries
- Serialize/deserialize for APIs
- Reduce coupling between layers
- Optimize data transfer

### MaritimeIQ DTOs

```csharp
// Request DTO
public class CreateVesselRequest
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public string IMONumber { get; set; }
    public VesselType Type { get; set; }
}

// Response DTO
public class VesselDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public string Status { get; set; }
    public PositionDto? CurrentPosition { get; set; }
}

// Mapping
public static class VesselMapper
{
    public static VesselDto ToDto(Vessel vessel)
    {
        return new VesselDto
        {
            Id = vessel.Id,
            Name = vessel.Name,
            Status = vessel.Status.ToString(),
            CurrentPosition = vessel.CurrentPosition?.ToDto()
        };
    }
}
```

