## 6. Validation

### Model Validation

**Data Annotations**:
```csharp
public class CreateVesselRequest
{
    [Required]
    [StringLength(100)]
    public string Name { get; set; }
    
    [Required]
    [RegularExpression(@"^\d{7}$")]
    public string IMONumber { get; set; }
    
    [Range(1, 1000)]
    public int PassengerCapacity { get; set; }
}
```

**Fluent Validation**:
```csharp
public class VesselValidator : AbstractValidator<Vessel>
{
    public VesselValidator()
    {
        RuleFor(v => v.Name)
            .NotEmpty()
            .MaximumLength(100);
        
        RuleFor(v => v.IMONumber)
            .NotEmpty()
            .Matches(@"^\d{7}$");
    }
}
```

**Business Rule Validation**:
```csharp
public void Activate()
{
    // Business rule validation
    if (Status == VesselStatus.Active)
        throw new InvalidOperationException("Vessel is already active");
    
    if (CurrentPosition == null)
        throw new InvalidOperationException("Vessel must have a position to activate");
    
    Status = VesselStatus.Active;
}
```

